    {
      "id": 99,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1300,
        500
      ],
      "size": [
        650,
        390
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 5,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Qwen Image 2.1 RGBA Edit — 40 steps\n\nStrict non-commercial use: research or evaluation only. Read the Qwen Research License: https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen-Image-2.1/blob/main/LICENSE\n\nSetup defaults: INT8 diffusion and encoder, native Qwen 2.1 BF16 VAE. Forced lossless PNG output with transparency (Save as WebP Conditional). Select models in the setup wizard.\n\nQwen editing keeps each reference at its source dimensions (encoder resolution=0, rounded to multiples of 32). Keep the encoder latent connected to the sampler. The source controls edit dimensions, not the Create megapixel selector. The save node forces lossless PNG for further edits. Larger sources cost more memory and time. Whole-image edits still reconstruct details; use an explicit edit mask to preserve unchanged pixels.\n\nUse a different sampler seed from the image's generation seed, including between successive edits. At the same dimensions, reusing that seed can cause Qwen 2.1 noise replay (grain and halos). Seed settings remain explicit and are not silently overridden."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# Qwen Image 2.1 RGBA Edit — 40 steps\n\nStrict non-commercial use: research or evaluation only. Read the Qwen Research License: https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen-Image-2.1/blob/main/LICENSE\n\nSetup defaults: INT8 diffusion and encoder, native Qwen 2.1 BF16 VAE. Forced lossless PNG output with transparency (Save as WebP Conditional). Select models in the setup wizard.\n\nQwen editing keeps each reference at its source dimensions (encoder resolution=0, rounded to multiples of 32). Keep the encoder latent connected to the sampler. The source controls edit dimensions, not the Create megapixel selector. The save node forces lossless PNG for further edits. Larger sources cost more memory and time. Whole-image edits still reconstruct details; use an explicit edit mask to preserve unchanged pixels.\n\nUse a different sampler seed from the image's generation seed, including between successive edits. At the same dimensions, reusing that seed can cause Qwen 2.1 noise replay (grain and halos). Seed settings remain explicit and are not silently overridden."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
